{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Feature Map.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Feature Map.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"convolutional feature map convolutional feature map","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Feature Map.md","fileName":"Convolutional Feature Map.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Convolutional Feature Map","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 02:14\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Convolutional Visual Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Convolutional Visual Architecture","Convolutional Kernel","Activation Function","CNN Pooling Layer","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Feature Map.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Feature Map.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"convolutional feature map convolutional feature map","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Feature Map.md","fileName":"Convolutional Feature Map.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Convolutional Feature Map","heading":"Convolutional Feature Map","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A feature map records the output of one [[Convolutional Kernel]] at each location where the kernel is applied. It is a spatial account of how strongly the learned local detector responded across an image, not merely a single yes-or-no answer for the whole image.\n\nA nonlinear [[Activation Function]] is commonly applied element by element to the map before a [[CNN Pooling Layer]] downsamples it. Maps from different kernels can also be combined and passed to a later convolutional layer. This lets the network build features from earlier detections while preserving spatial information until the architecture chooses to reduce it.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Convolutional Visual Architecture","Convolutional Kernel","Activation Function","CNN Pooling Layer","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Feature Map.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Feature Map.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"convolutional feature map convolutional feature map","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Convolutional Feature Map.md","fileName":"Convolutional Feature Map.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Convolutional Feature Map","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Convolutional Visual Architecture","Convolutional Kernel","Activation Function","CNN Pooling Layer","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}